    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0096" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McKelvey</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-09T15:00:00+08:00">February 9, 1948—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 9—9:05 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Communists capture Liaoyang (mytel 66 to Department February 5<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d65-f1"/>) confirmed. Government losses inside Liaoyang not
                    known-One Government division attempting break siege, flanked by Communists and
                    reported two of three Government regiments lost.</p>
                <p>Sent Embassy as 105; repeated Department as 71, Tientsin 54, Peiping 58.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McKelvey</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
